Metric:
- id: scaling.effectiveness
- name: 
- description: This metric measures the effectiveness of autoscaling mechanisms in cloud infrastructure by evaluating the timeliness and adequacy of scaling actions in response to the target load. It assesses how quickly resources are scaled up or down to meet demand, ensuring that performance remains optimal without incurring unnecessary costs. The metric also considers whether the scaling actions are sufficient to handle the actual load, preventing both under-provisioning and over-provisioning scenarios. By analyzing this metric, organizations can identify potential bottlenecks in their scaling processes and optimize resource allocation. Ultimately, it helps in maintaining a balance between performance, cost efficiency, and resource utilization.

