Metric:
- id: lb.performance
- name: 
- description: This metric measures the performance of load balancers by tracking request latency and error rates in relation to defined Service Level Objectives (SLOs). It provides insights into how quickly requests are processed and the frequency of errors encountered during load balancing operations. By comparing these metrics against established SLOs, organizations can assess whether their load balancers are meeting performance expectations. This measurement is crucial for ensuring optimal user experience and application reliability. Additionally, it helps identify potential bottlenecks or issues in the infrastructure that may require attention to maintain service quality.

