Metric:
- id: cost.idle_underutilized
- name: 
- description: This metric measures the proportion of cloud spending that is associated with resources that are either idle or underutilized. Idle resources are those that are provisioned but not actively used, while underutilized resources are those that are not operating at their full capacity. By quantifying this share of spending, organizations can identify inefficiencies in their cloud infrastructure and operations. The scope of this metric includes virtual machines, storage, and other cloud services that may be over-provisioned or not optimally configured. Understanding this metric is crucial for effective cost management and resource optimization in cloud environments.

