Metric:
- id: cost.allocation_quality
- name: 
- description: This metric measures the accuracy of cloud spending attribution to specific teams or services within an organization. It assesses how well cloud costs are tagged and categorized, ensuring that expenses are correctly aligned with the responsible entities. High allocation quality indicates that teams can effectively track their cloud usage and associated costs, facilitating better financial accountability and decision-making. Conversely, low allocation quality may lead to misinformed budgeting and resource allocation, impacting overall cloud governance. This metric is crucial for optimizing cloud expenditure and enhancing the financial operations (FinOps) strategy.

